      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "locality ↑",
      "description": "COHERENCE. Share of the last 50 commits whose changes stay inside one module (directory depth 2). Higher is better. Low or falling values mean a typical change cuts across module boundaries: the boundaries no longer match how the code changes. Evidence: the variable encapsulation metrics were validated against; follow-on patch size predicted agent failure. Gaming: splitting one change into several single-module commits; measure per merged PR.",
